    stem: "2023 Part B 新题型：根据材料完成 41–45 题。",
    referenceAnswer: "【总体分析】\n\n本文为观点匹配题，选自《卫报》，主题为英国新建筑法规对房价和建筑成本的影响。文章首先介绍新规内容及其目标，随后引用多位行业专家的观点，分别从成本上升、具体限制、短期影响和长期效益等角度展开分析。\n\n【题目解析】\n\n41. Brian Berry\n【答案】 [D] The new rules will take home prices to an even higher level.\n【解析】\n定位至第四段。Brian Berry指出，新规要求使用新材料、新测试方法和新系统，而当前价格已经“sky high”，消费者将“have to pay more”。选项[D]中的“take home prices to an even higher level”与此处“pay more”语义一致，均指向新规将进一步推高房价。\n\n42. Gareth Belsham\n【答案】 [F] The new rules will affect people whose home extensions include new windows or doors.\n【解析】\n定位至第五段。Gareth Belsham指出，翻新或扩建房屋的人将“directly affected”，并特别强调“any new windows or doors must be highly insulated”。选项[F]中“affect people whose home extensions include new windows or doors”与原文内容高度吻合，属于原词复现与语义对应。\n\n43. Marcus Jefford\n【答案】 [B] Builders possibly need to submit new estimates of their projects.\n【解析】\n定位至第九段。Marcus Jefford提到，已估算成本但未提交文件的建筑商“may need to go back and submit fresh estimates”。选项[B]中“submit new estimates”与原文“submit fresh estimates”为同义替换，且主语“builders”一致，内容完全对应。\n\n44. John Kelly\n【答案】 [A] The rise of home prices is a temporary matter.\n【解析】\n定位至第十一段。John Kelly认为价格“will eventually come down”，但“not in the immediate future”，即短期内仍需承担转型成本。选项[A]中“a temporary matter”是对“eventually come down”的合理推断，强调房价上涨是暂时的。\n\n45. Andrew Mellor\n【答案】 [G] The rule changes will benefit homeowners eventually.\n【解析】\n定位至最后一段。Andrew Mellor指出，长期来看新规将带来更舒适、节能的住房，房主“will recoup that cost over time in energy bill savings”，并明确提到“they will have that benefit over time”。选项[G]中“benefit homeowners eventually”与原文“benefit over time”直接对应，属于原词复现与语义一致。",
